{"seconds": 74.1, "exit": 0, "final": "Great, Qxh7# is still mate. So the main line is:\n\n1. **Nef6+** \n\nAnd Black's best tries all lose to mate:\n- 1...Kh8 2. Qxh7# \n- 1...Qxf6 2. Qxh7# \n- 1...Nxf6 2. Nxf6+ Kh8 3. Qxh7# (or 2. Qxh7+ first also works)\n- 1...Bxf6 2. Qxh7# \n- 1...gxf6 2. Qxh7#\n\nThis is a **discovered attack** combined with a **fork** and **back rank mate** pattern. The knight move gives check, discovers an attack on the d5 knight from the queen, and sets up an unstoppable mating attack on h7.\n\n**Coaching note for the club player:**\n\nThe winning move is **Nef6+**. After this forcing check, White has an unstoppable mating attack on h7 (Qxh7#). The key insight: move your knight to give check AND unblock your queen's line to a key square. When your opponent is under time pressure, forcing checks that also improve your position are often the right move. Always look for \"doing two things at once\"\u2014here, the check pulls the king where you want it, while the discovered attack on the loose knight on d5 secures your attack.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nef6+\", \"line\": [\"Nef6+\", \"Kh8\", \"Qxh7#\"], \"motifs\": [\"discoveredAttack\", \"fork\", \"backRankMate\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2q1rk1/p4ppp/4p3/3n3N/3nN2b/3Q1P2/PPBp2KP/R6R w - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2q1rk1/p4ppp/4p3/3n3N/3nN2b/3Q1P2/PPBp2KP/R6R w - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2q1rk1/p4ppp/4p3/3n3N/3nN2b/3Q1P2/PPBp2KP/R6R w - - 0 23", "square": "h4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2q1rk1/p4ppp/4p3/3n3N/3nN2b/3Q1P2/PPBp2KP/R6R w - - 0 23", "square": "d5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2q1rk1/p4ppp/4p3/3n3N/3nN2b/3Q1P2/PPBp2KP/R6R w - - 0 23", "square": "d4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2q1rk1/p4ppp/4p3/3n3N/3nN2b/3Q1P2/PPBp2KP/R6R w - - 0 23", "square"